- Tax is rounded *up* to the minor unit. That is what tax authorities require, and what naive
- rounding gets wrong in exactly the cases which matter. Twenty per cent of £2.94 is £0.588,
- which is charged as £0.59:
+ O imposto é arredondado *para cima* até a unidade menor. É isso que as autoridades fiscais
+ exigem, e é o que o arredondamento ingênuo erra exatamente nos casos que importam. Vinte por cento
+ de £2,94 são £0,588, que é cobrado como £0,59:

= which is charged as £0.59:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= which is charged as £0.59:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= which is charged as £0.59:
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
